Drag inside a clip's box to move it. Every selected clip moves by the same amount and keeps its place relative to the others, including a selected clip that isn't at the playhead. Clips on locked tracks stay where they are.

The move [snaps](/canvas/canvas-snapping/) to the canvas and to other layers. Snapping goes by the clip you grabbed, so the whole selection clicks into place together.

## Nudge

To shift a clip by an exact number of pixels, type a new value into **Position X** or **Position Y** on the [Picture tab](/canvas/transform/).

The arrow keys don't move a clip on the canvas, even with the canvas focused. They keep their usual job: <kbd>←</kbd> and <kbd>→</kbd> step the playhead by a frame, <kbd>⇧←</kbd> and <kbd>⇧→</kbd> by ten, and <kbd>↑</kbd> and <kbd>↓</kbd> go to the previous and next edit point.

To shift a clip earlier or later in time, see [Nudge clips](/editing/nudge-clips/).

